WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.250
So who's my guest this week?

00:00:02.250 --> 00:00:05.430
It's the US Attorney, Gloria Allred.

00:00:05.430 --> 00:00:08.400
She calls herself an
avenger for women's rights,

00:00:08.400 --> 00:00:12.270
and one glance at her CV gives
that claim serious weight.

00:00:12.270 --> 00:00:13.680
Over the last 40 years,

00:00:13.680 --> 00:00:15.930
if there's been a high
profile sexual assault case

00:00:15.930 --> 00:00:18.840
in America, it's likely
Allred's been the lawyer

00:00:18.840 --> 00:00:20.730
for some of the victims.

00:00:20.730 --> 00:00:22.920
A lifelong campaigner for equality,

00:00:22.920 --> 00:00:26.670
she represented Roe after
the Roe V. Wade case.

00:00:26.670 --> 00:00:28.110
She's not without her critics,

00:00:28.110 --> 00:00:32.370
who say she's as interested in
publicity as she is justice,

00:00:32.370 --> 00:00:35.010
but undeterred at 81 years old,

00:00:35.010 --> 00:00:38.250
she has no intention of retiring.

00:00:38.250 --> 00:00:41.730
So as America grapples
with abortion rights again,

00:00:41.730 --> 00:00:44.643
what does she make of
that Supreme Court ruling?

00:00:45.720 --> 00:00:48.090
Here's a taste of what's coming up.

00:00:48.090 --> 00:00:51.120
In 2020, you hired a
yellow American school bus

00:00:51.120 --> 00:00:53.130
to drive around London,
near Buckingham Palace.

00:00:53.130 --> 00:00:54.907
Prince Andrew's face
was on it with a sign,

00:00:54.907 --> 00:00:57.187
"If you see this man, please
ask him to call the FBI

00:00:57.187 --> 00:00:58.890
to answer their questions."

00:00:58.890 --> 00:01:02.610
Is that matter now closed
or are there other avenues?

00:01:02.610 --> 00:01:07.610
He to this day has never
agreed to sit with the FBI.

00:01:09.660 --> 00:01:12.690
He should be ashamed of himself

00:01:12.690 --> 00:01:15.120
that he refuses to do it.

00:01:15.120 --> 00:01:16.380
He's avoided.

00:01:16.380 --> 00:01:17.670
He's evaded.

00:01:17.670 --> 00:01:19.323
He's escaped doing it.

00:01:33.060 --> 00:01:35.760
Gloria Allred, thank you
so much for talking to me

00:01:35.760 --> 00:01:37.710
for taking some time out
of your busy schedule.

00:01:37.710 --> 00:01:39.480
It's wonderful to be able

00:01:39.480 --> 00:01:41.880
to talk to you about such
a range of issues today.

00:01:41.880 --> 00:01:46.770
And of course, America and
women's rights are global news.

00:01:46.770 --> 00:01:48.990
And I wanted to start by asking you,

00:01:48.990 --> 00:01:51.810
are you proud to be an
American at the moment?

00:01:51.810 --> 00:01:54.240
Well, I'm always very grateful

00:01:54.240 --> 00:01:59.240
that my mother came from
the UK to the United States,

00:02:00.210 --> 00:02:02.610
and that I was able to grow up here.

00:02:02.610 --> 00:02:06.750
And I do have a lot of confidence

00:02:06.750 --> 00:02:11.750
in our system of justice and of rights,

00:02:11.820 --> 00:02:14.730
but I'm very, very disappointed.

00:02:14.730 --> 00:02:19.730
I'm very outraged about
what has happened recently

00:02:19.890 --> 00:02:22.560
with the United States
Supreme Court decision

00:02:22.560 --> 00:02:25.110
in Roe V. Wade,

00:02:25.110 --> 00:02:30.110
but it was inevitable
given some serious flaws

00:02:30.840 --> 00:02:31.800
in our system.

00:02:31.800 --> 00:02:33.960
Yes, that's what's been talked about

00:02:33.960 --> 00:02:36.000
in terms of the way the
justices are appointed,

00:02:36.000 --> 00:02:37.590
the political leanings.

00:02:37.590 --> 00:02:40.530
I suppose I wanted to ask
you also with that decision

00:02:40.530 --> 00:02:43.740
as an attorney, do you have
any sympathy with the view

00:02:43.740 --> 00:02:47.100
that abortion shouldn't have
been a constitutional right?

00:02:47.100 --> 00:02:51.510
And that there may be merit
in having state-by-state laws?

00:02:51.510 --> 00:02:55.320
There's absolutely no merit whatsoever

00:02:55.320 --> 00:03:00.320
in throwing the decision
that a woman should

00:03:01.650 --> 00:03:06.303
or should not be able to have
an abortion to the states.

00:03:07.260 --> 00:03:11.760
It should, and has been
a constitutional right

00:03:11.760 --> 00:03:16.760
for a woman to choose whether
or not to bear a pregnancy.

00:03:16.980 --> 00:03:21.980
And that has been the law ever since 1973,

00:03:22.121 --> 00:03:25.260
when Roe V. Wade was decided

00:03:25.260 --> 00:03:27.720
by the United States Supreme Court.

00:03:27.720 --> 00:03:30.640
And that a woman did
have a right to choose

00:03:31.920 --> 00:03:35.430
whether or not to continue
with her pregnancy,

00:03:35.430 --> 00:03:40.320
at least at certain
stages of her pregnancy.

00:03:40.320 --> 00:03:42.120
It's very dangerous.

00:03:42.120 --> 00:03:44.010
It is barbaric.

00:03:44.010 --> 00:03:49.010
It is just an outrage and cruel

00:03:49.380 --> 00:03:54.030
to throw this decision to the states.

00:03:54.030 --> 00:03:56.130
I'll give you an example, Emma.

00:03:56.130 --> 00:03:57.300
Okay, yes, please.

00:03:57.300 --> 00:04:00.741
Prior to 1973 and

00:04:00.741 --> 00:04:04.770
prior to Roe V. Wade decision,

00:04:04.770 --> 00:04:09.270
many states were criminalizing abortion.

00:04:09.270 --> 00:04:14.107
So, young women like me
who were in their '20s

00:04:15.390 --> 00:04:17.820
and had no resources

00:04:17.820 --> 00:04:22.380
would have to try to
gather some money to pay

00:04:22.380 --> 00:04:25.740
someone to provide a back alley abortion.

00:04:25.740 --> 00:04:30.540
So I was raped at gunpoint in Mexico

00:04:30.540 --> 00:04:32.340
when I went there for a vacation,

00:04:32.340 --> 00:04:34.503
when I came back to California,

00:04:35.760 --> 00:04:38.220
this was in the late '60s,

00:04:38.220 --> 00:04:40.560
I found that I was pregnant

00:04:40.560 --> 00:04:43.170
and that it was a crime for anyone

00:04:43.170 --> 00:04:47.490
to assist with an abortion in California.

00:04:47.490 --> 00:04:49.260
So I had to get some money together

00:04:49.260 --> 00:04:54.260
for a back alley abortionist
who did provide the abortion,

00:04:54.360 --> 00:04:58.200
but left me in a bathtub hemorrhaging

00:04:58.200 --> 00:05:01.170
in a pool of my own blood.

00:05:01.170 --> 00:05:06.170
And he said that he could not
help me after the abortion.

00:05:07.380 --> 00:05:11.280
911 was called to take me to the hospital.

00:05:11.280 --> 00:05:14.340
And there I was taken to a unit

00:05:14.340 --> 00:05:18.540
where they would try
to save a woman's life

00:05:18.540 --> 00:05:21.783
if she was hemorrhaging from an abortion.

00:05:22.980 --> 00:05:25.200
The police came and interviewed me,

00:05:25.200 --> 00:05:27.220
which was very frightening to me

00:05:28.230 --> 00:05:33.230
because I didn't know if
the name I would give them

00:05:33.540 --> 00:05:36.900
would be the name of the
real person who provided it,

00:05:36.900 --> 00:05:39.120
or if I should give a name at all

00:05:39.120 --> 00:05:41.520
for fear that he would do something to me

00:05:41.520 --> 00:05:43.563
if I gave the name, which I didn't.

00:05:44.910 --> 00:05:48.090
I was packed in ice, I
had 106 degree fever.

00:05:48.090 --> 00:05:52.260
I almost died from an illegal abortion,

00:05:52.260 --> 00:05:56.347
and the nurse who was
anti-choice said to me,

00:05:56.347 --> 00:05:59.190
"I hope this teaches you a lesson."

00:05:59.190 --> 00:06:02.640
And I say that it did teach me a lesson.

00:06:02.640 --> 00:06:07.640
And the lesson is that abortion
should be safe and legal

00:06:07.650 --> 00:06:10.650
and available and affordable,

00:06:10.650 --> 00:06:15.650
and no woman or girl should
have to risk her life

00:06:15.900 --> 00:06:17.730
with an illegal abortion.

00:06:17.730 --> 00:06:18.930
I was just going to say,

00:06:18.930 --> 00:06:20.580
and thank you for sharing that.

00:06:20.580 --> 00:06:22.890
I know you've spoken
about your experiences

00:06:22.890 --> 00:06:27.420
because they are very
relevant and highly traumatic

00:06:27.420 --> 00:06:29.610
and you don't want to
go back to that place.

00:06:29.610 --> 00:06:31.320
But one of the arguments mounted

00:06:31.320 --> 00:06:34.200
by those who are in favor
of this decision is,

00:06:34.200 --> 00:06:37.860
well, women can travel,
women can go to other states,

00:06:37.860 --> 00:06:39.870
but of course, if they
don't have the means

00:06:39.870 --> 00:06:41.130
like you are saying,

00:06:41.130 --> 00:06:44.070
and they don't have the
wherewithal or can't get in touch

00:06:44.070 --> 00:06:47.220
with those who can help them,
then they won't be able to.

00:06:47.220 --> 00:06:48.780
And I just wanted to ask you,

00:06:48.780 --> 00:06:51.240
are you expecting as an attorney

00:06:51.240 --> 00:06:55.020
to have some clients now who come to you

00:06:55.020 --> 00:06:58.440
who may end up, this hasn't
happened yet being prosecuted

00:06:58.440 --> 00:07:01.440
for either ordering abortion pills online

00:07:01.440 --> 00:07:04.200
or trying to cross state boundaries?

00:07:04.200 --> 00:07:06.630
How concerned are you about that?

00:07:06.630 --> 00:07:10.890
Well, you raise another very
important issue, actually,

00:07:10.890 --> 00:07:12.510
a number of important issues.

00:07:12.510 --> 00:07:17.160
So for example, you just
mentioned medication abortions.

00:07:17.160 --> 00:07:20.820
Medication abortions are about half

00:07:20.820 --> 00:07:24.450
of all of the abortions
in the United States.

00:07:24.450 --> 00:07:28.590
The anti-choice movement,
the movement that believes

00:07:28.590 --> 00:07:31.950
that a fertilized egg
should have more rights

00:07:31.950 --> 00:07:35.700
than an adult woman is trying to interfere

00:07:35.700 --> 00:07:38.400
with medication abortions.

00:07:38.400 --> 00:07:42.450
For example, to suggest to legislators

00:07:42.450 --> 00:07:44.970
that the pill can only be sent

00:07:44.970 --> 00:07:47.520
if a doctor is seen in person,

00:07:47.520 --> 00:07:50.610
which many women are not able to do,

00:07:50.610 --> 00:07:52.770
it also invades their privacy

00:07:52.770 --> 00:07:57.630
because we are also concerned
by the anti-choice forces,

00:07:57.630 --> 00:08:00.600
trying to obtain medical records,

00:08:00.600 --> 00:08:03.810
to find out when a woman is menstruating.

00:08:03.810 --> 00:08:07.705
You also mentioned the right
to travel to other states,

00:08:07.705 --> 00:08:10.320
Emma, that's a significant issue.

00:08:10.320 --> 00:08:15.150
There are many poor women
who can't afford childcare.

00:08:15.150 --> 00:08:19.920
These are just some of the
problems that are now existing

00:08:19.920 --> 00:08:22.410
for a woman to travel to another state.

00:08:22.410 --> 00:08:26.460
Of course, wealthy women
will always be able to travel

00:08:26.460 --> 00:08:27.360
to another state

00:08:27.360 --> 00:08:31.320
or another country like
Canada to get an abortion.

00:08:31.320 --> 00:08:34.920
Indeed, and on those issues and

00:08:34.920 --> 00:08:37.920
the complications that are going to arise,

00:08:37.920 --> 00:08:41.910
do you think Joe Biden has
done enough to demonstrate

00:08:41.910 --> 00:08:44.640
to the women of America
who are of your view

00:08:44.640 --> 00:08:48.180
and are worried about this,
that this is not okay,

00:08:48.180 --> 00:08:52.440
that this is not the America
that he wants to preside over?

00:08:52.440 --> 00:08:53.820
Has he done enough?

00:08:53.820 --> 00:08:56.400
I think that the President knows

00:08:56.400 --> 00:09:01.400
that there are so many challenges
now facing women and girls

00:09:01.650 --> 00:09:04.170
because of this dangerous decision,

00:09:04.170 --> 00:09:09.120
he has very limited
ability to do anything.

00:09:09.120 --> 00:09:11.070
The main challenge

00:09:11.070 --> 00:09:16.070
is that we're going to have
to get everyone to come out

00:09:16.170 --> 00:09:19.110
to vote in the upcoming election.

00:09:19.110 --> 00:09:24.110
We must remember in November
is our Clarion call.

00:09:24.480 --> 00:09:27.480
Our Clarion cry for justice.

00:09:27.480 --> 00:09:29.190
What that means is,

00:09:29.190 --> 00:09:33.090
that pro-choice voters
are going to have to vote

00:09:33.090 --> 00:09:36.360
in both federal and state elections

00:09:36.360 --> 00:09:39.750
for pro-choice elected officials.

00:09:39.750 --> 00:09:43.020
And we must throw out of office

00:09:43.020 --> 00:09:47.160
the anti-choice compulsory pregnancy crowd

00:09:47.160 --> 00:09:52.160
that is passing these
restrictive and dangerous laws

00:09:52.710 --> 00:09:57.710
in the states and also is
causing essentially paralysis

00:09:58.680 --> 00:10:01.590
in the Congress and the
United States Senate.

00:10:01.590 --> 00:10:05.850
We must elect more pro-choice
United States senators

00:10:05.850 --> 00:10:10.530
and representatives in the house
of representatives as well.

00:10:10.530 --> 00:10:14.220
I was minded to bring up to
you a very striking remark

00:10:14.220 --> 00:10:16.410
she's known for them - from Fran Lebowitz,

00:10:16.410 --> 00:10:17.970
the writer and commentator.

00:10:17.970 --> 00:10:20.610
She's recently compared
the Republican Party

00:10:20.610 --> 00:10:25.020
to the Taliban regarding
control over women's bodies.

00:10:25.020 --> 00:10:27.480
What do you make of that comparison?

00:10:27.480 --> 00:10:29.643
Well, I can understand why she said it.

00:10:30.480 --> 00:10:33.690
Because this is controlling
women's choices and their lives.

00:10:33.690 --> 00:10:38.580
It's often been said, Emma,
that if we can't control,

00:10:38.580 --> 00:10:42.660
if we cannot control our
lives from the skin in,

00:10:42.660 --> 00:10:46.440
we cannot control our
lives from the skin out.

00:10:46.440 --> 00:10:50.760
And this is about even more
than reproductive choice

00:10:50.760 --> 00:10:54.060
because not being able
to choose what we do

00:10:54.060 --> 00:10:55.830
with our own bodies

00:10:55.830 --> 00:10:58.557
means that there is
going to be interference

00:10:58.557 --> 00:11:01.350
with our educational opportunities,

00:11:01.350 --> 00:11:05.790
our business opportunities,
our physical opportunities,

00:11:05.790 --> 00:11:08.070
our emotional opportunities,

00:11:08.070 --> 00:11:12.030
and it is going to have a draconian impact

00:11:12.030 --> 00:11:14.760
on each and every woman's life.

00:11:14.760 --> 00:11:16.170
We cannot go back.

00:11:16.170 --> 00:11:18.180
We will not go back

00:11:18.180 --> 00:11:22.080
and we must have a passion to fight back,

00:11:22.080 --> 00:11:24.750
to win back our rights.

00:11:24.750 --> 00:11:26.910
I wanted to just come to Norma McCorvey,

00:11:26.910 --> 00:11:31.590
who was Roe in this case,
you later represented her.

00:11:31.590 --> 00:11:34.050
You worked with her, but she later,

00:11:34.050 --> 00:11:37.200
despite having become once
her name was known synonymous

00:11:37.200 --> 00:11:41.231
with this case that granted
women until recently,

00:11:41.231 --> 00:11:43.650
constitutional rights to abortion,

00:11:43.650 --> 00:11:45.450
she changed sides publicly.

00:11:45.450 --> 00:11:47.340
She went against choice.

00:11:47.340 --> 00:11:51.150
She went against abortion,
and then it was revealed

00:11:51.150 --> 00:11:54.330
that she'd been paid by
that side of the debate

00:11:54.330 --> 00:11:57.000
to assume that position
just before she died,

00:11:57.000 --> 00:11:58.680
that was revealed.

00:11:58.680 --> 00:12:00.960
Did you know she had been paid?

00:12:00.960 --> 00:12:03.030
And what did you make
of that whole episode,

00:12:03.030 --> 00:12:06.300
having known the woman
who was known as Roe?

00:12:06.300 --> 00:12:09.330
Look, every woman gets to make the choice

00:12:09.330 --> 00:12:11.160
that she wants to make.

00:12:11.160 --> 00:12:13.590
I don't control any woman's choice.

00:12:13.590 --> 00:12:15.930
I don't try to do that.

00:12:15.930 --> 00:12:18.840
That's what the anti-choice people do.

00:12:18.840 --> 00:12:21.600
So yes, was it disappointing?

00:12:21.600 --> 00:12:25.740
Of course, but did I try to coerce her?

00:12:25.740 --> 00:12:28.050
That's not my role.

00:12:28.050 --> 00:12:30.090
It's not anybody's role,

00:12:30.090 --> 00:12:31.980
but she admitted the truth in the end.

00:12:31.980 --> 00:12:33.390
I'm glad that she did it.

00:12:33.390 --> 00:12:36.150
Let me bring you to
another area of your work

00:12:36.150 --> 00:12:39.000
which is representing victims

00:12:39.000 --> 00:12:41.280
of sexual abuse and sexual assault.

00:12:41.280 --> 00:12:43.440
Because recently Ghislaine Maxwell

00:12:43.440 --> 00:12:44.970
was sentenced to 20 years

00:12:44.970 --> 00:12:48.990
for recruiting and trafficking
14 girls for sexual abuse,

00:12:48.990 --> 00:12:53.040
of course, in connection
to Jeffrey Epstein.

00:12:53.040 --> 00:12:57.180
It's very striking although
a woman has gone to prison,

00:12:57.180 --> 00:13:02.180
but we still don't know the
names of the other men involved.

00:13:02.250 --> 00:13:06.090
Yeah, I have no idea what
the prosecutors have in mind.

00:13:06.090 --> 00:13:08.640
Federal prosecutors hold their cards

00:13:08.640 --> 00:13:11.400
very, very close to their vest.

00:13:11.400 --> 00:13:12.930
And they're known for that.

00:13:12.930 --> 00:13:16.830
So I have no idea what
they're planning next

00:13:16.830 --> 00:13:19.750
or if they're planning anything else

00:13:21.870 --> 00:13:25.710
in reference to prosecuting
any other individuals

00:13:25.710 --> 00:13:29.490
who might have been
involved with Ms. Maxwell

00:13:29.490 --> 00:13:31.290
and with Jeffrey Epstein.

00:13:31.290 --> 00:13:33.150
And just following on from that again

00:13:33.150 --> 00:13:34.740
about whether something is closed

00:13:34.740 --> 00:13:37.530
or there could be further actions

00:13:37.530 --> 00:13:39.930
because of your experience
I wanted to ask you,

00:13:39.930 --> 00:13:41.280
but also because of something you did,

00:13:41.280 --> 00:13:42.960
and coming to Prince Andrew,

00:13:42.960 --> 00:13:46.020
in 2020 you hired a
yellow American school bus

00:13:46.020 --> 00:13:48.060
to drive around London,
near Buckingham Palace.

00:13:48.060 --> 00:13:49.200
I know you remember it.

00:13:49.200 --> 00:13:50.310
Some others will remember it.

00:13:50.310 --> 00:13:52.657
Prince Andrew's face was
on it, saying with a sign.

00:13:52.657 --> 00:13:53.880
"If you see this man,

00:13:53.880 --> 00:13:56.670
please ask him to call the FBI
to answer their questions."

00:13:56.670 --> 00:13:58.860
And as you say, because
you were representing

00:13:58.860 --> 00:14:01.290
some of Jeffrey Epstein's victims.

00:14:01.290 --> 00:14:03.570
Earlier this year, Prince
Andrew did come to a settlement

00:14:03.570 --> 00:14:05.820
with Virginia Giuffre,

00:14:05.820 --> 00:14:08.370
Prince Andrew's always
denied any wrongdoing.

00:14:08.370 --> 00:14:12.330
Is that matter now closed
or are there other avenues?

00:14:12.330 --> 00:14:17.330
I did that because I wanted
Prince Andrew to cooperate

00:14:17.910 --> 00:14:21.771
and give an interview to the FBI

00:14:21.771 --> 00:14:25.440
about what he knew about Jeffrey Epstein.

00:14:25.440 --> 00:14:28.050
Anything else they
wanted to ask about him?

00:14:28.050 --> 00:14:29.490
Since Prince Andrew stayed

00:14:29.490 --> 00:14:33.540
in many residences
owned by Jeffrey Epstein

00:14:33.540 --> 00:14:38.460
and where young girls were
present, he never did that.

00:14:38.460 --> 00:14:42.450
In other words, he gave
an interview to the BBC.

00:14:42.450 --> 00:14:45.360
That of course was not under oath.

00:14:45.360 --> 00:14:49.890
And it was a complete catastrophe
from a PR point of view.

00:14:49.890 --> 00:14:53.400
I wanted him to sit with the FBI

00:14:53.400 --> 00:14:56.640
and testify under oath or
even if not under oath,

00:14:56.640 --> 00:14:59.910
his duty legally would
be to tell the truth

00:14:59.910 --> 00:15:02.880
which he had no duty to do to the BBC,

00:15:02.880 --> 00:15:05.070
although it would've been nice.

00:15:05.070 --> 00:15:06.753
Don't know if he did it or not.

00:15:07.650 --> 00:15:09.810
He never did it.

00:15:09.810 --> 00:15:12.660
The civil settlement that you mentioned

00:15:12.660 --> 00:15:16.170
had nothing to do with the criminal case

00:15:16.170 --> 00:15:19.830
being prosecuted against Ms. Maxwell,

00:15:19.830 --> 00:15:22.890
and nothing to do with anything

00:15:22.890 --> 00:15:25.470
but the criminal justice system,

00:15:25.470 --> 00:15:30.162
he to this day has never agreed

00:15:30.162 --> 00:15:32.412
to sit with the FBI.

00:15:32.412 --> 00:15:35.580
He should be ashamed of himself,

00:15:35.580 --> 00:15:39.090
that he refuses to do it, he's avoided.

00:15:39.090 --> 00:15:42.718
he's evaded, he's escaped doing it.

00:15:42.718 --> 00:15:47.718
Now the criminal case against
Ms. Maxwell will go on appeal,

00:15:47.728 --> 00:15:51.870
but I say it's never too late

00:15:51.870 --> 00:15:53.880
for him to sit with the prosecutors.

00:15:53.880 --> 00:15:58.880
They themselves said that he
was not providing an interview.

00:15:59.220 --> 00:16:00.634
You are saying,

00:16:00.634 --> 00:16:01.740
you know he didn't sit down with the FBI,

00:16:01.740 --> 00:16:03.750
that's what's understood.

00:16:03.750 --> 00:16:06.750
And why should he still
have a conversation

00:16:06.750 --> 00:16:09.150
with the FBI to help which case?

00:16:09.150 --> 00:16:11.640
Well, it could open up new cases

00:16:11.640 --> 00:16:14.760
that is provide evidence for new cases.

00:16:14.760 --> 00:16:19.760
So look, anyone who may
have any information

00:16:20.340 --> 00:16:22.320
that is relevant

00:16:22.320 --> 00:16:27.180
to crimes against
children should volunteer

00:16:27.180 --> 00:16:31.770
to speak to law enforcement,
FBI, state law enforcement,

00:16:31.770 --> 00:16:36.770
anywhere else, not have to be
dragged kicking and screaming

00:16:36.840 --> 00:16:39.270
or just try to avoid it completely.

00:16:39.270 --> 00:16:42.060
Perhaps he would say he
doesn't have any information.

00:16:42.060 --> 00:16:44.550
He's not here to speak
to what you are saying,

00:16:44.550 --> 00:16:47.070
he has always denied
wrongdoing, but perhaps-

00:16:47.070 --> 00:16:48.330
Well, that's complete...

00:16:48.330 --> 00:16:49.680
That's perhaps his reason.

00:16:49.680 --> 00:16:53.850
That is complete and utter nonsense,

00:16:53.850 --> 00:16:58.140
that he has no information whatsoever.

00:16:58.140 --> 00:17:02.250
He stayed in the residence
of Jeffrey Epstein

00:17:02.250 --> 00:17:06.150
with Jeffrey Epstein when
young girls were coming

00:17:06.150 --> 00:17:09.600
and going from that
residence in Manhattan,

00:17:09.600 --> 00:17:13.038
he also visited other residences

00:17:13.038 --> 00:17:16.350
of Jeffrey Epstein, other properties.

00:17:16.350 --> 00:17:21.350
We know that, that's a matter
of fact, not speculation,

00:17:21.420 --> 00:17:26.420
to say that he has no
information is just not true.

00:17:26.730 --> 00:17:31.080
And even he has not dared to say it.

00:17:31.080 --> 00:17:33.240
It's completely false.

00:17:33.240 --> 00:17:36.840
Gloria, when you are
on the case for people,

00:17:36.840 --> 00:17:39.720
largely it's been women, lots
of the cases you work on,

00:17:39.720 --> 00:17:40.620
we never hear about,

00:17:40.620 --> 00:17:43.590
but there are some very
high profile cases,

00:17:43.590 --> 00:17:46.320
you are known for your ability,

00:17:46.320 --> 00:17:49.080
your mastery to get attention,

00:17:49.080 --> 00:17:51.810
to pull stunts to call press conferences,

00:17:51.810 --> 00:17:53.010
whether it's a school bus,

00:17:53.010 --> 00:17:54.990
whether it's get people
in front of a camera,

00:17:54.990 --> 00:17:57.180
I'm sure you have to work
with those women as well

00:17:57.180 --> 00:17:59.976
to get them ready for
those sorts of situations.

00:17:59.976 --> 00:18:02.520
What do you make of some of the criticism

00:18:02.520 --> 00:18:06.510
that you have faced about that approach,

00:18:06.510 --> 00:18:09.630
that being one of your
hallmarks, if you like?

00:18:09.630 --> 00:18:12.250
Emma, there are many people who think

00:18:13.230 --> 00:18:16.560
that women should have
to suffer in silence.

00:18:16.560 --> 00:18:18.180
I'm not one of them.

00:18:18.180 --> 00:18:21.150
I think that women should have a voice.

00:18:21.150 --> 00:18:24.600
They should be able to
speak truth to power.

00:18:24.600 --> 00:18:27.990
They should be able to speak out

00:18:27.990 --> 00:18:32.990
about the injustices against
them in an appropriate case,

00:18:33.090 --> 00:18:35.790
depending on what their goal is.

00:18:35.790 --> 00:18:38.580
And only after they've been advised

00:18:38.580 --> 00:18:41.970
of the benefits and
risks of that decision,

00:18:41.970 --> 00:18:43.620
which is what I do.

00:18:43.620 --> 00:18:46.770
Have you been disappointed at points

00:18:46.770 --> 00:18:49.410
by some of the men that
you've come up against

00:18:49.410 --> 00:18:51.690
because maybe you were
a fan of their work,

00:18:51.690 --> 00:18:53.310
you'd enjoyed their music,

00:18:53.310 --> 00:18:56.460
you'd watch their, I don't
know, sporting performance,

00:18:56.460 --> 00:18:57.480
have you had that moment

00:18:57.480 --> 00:18:59.550
that some people have when
they hear about somebody,

00:18:59.550 --> 00:19:00.420
when they're found guilty

00:19:00.420 --> 00:19:03.120
and they thought "no, not that person".

00:19:03.120 --> 00:19:04.800
Have you had that?

00:19:04.800 --> 00:19:06.150
Not really.

00:19:06.150 --> 00:19:06.983
No?

00:19:06.983 --> 00:19:11.983
Because I'm just very
goal-oriented for my clients

00:19:12.270 --> 00:19:13.830
who are victims.

00:19:13.830 --> 00:19:18.830
I know that many celebrities
lead double lives

00:19:19.530 --> 00:19:23.550
or triple lives where the character

00:19:23.550 --> 00:19:26.520
or the brand that they've created

00:19:26.520 --> 00:19:30.270
are not who they are in real life.

00:19:30.270 --> 00:19:33.810
And so I don't buy into the fantasy.

00:19:33.810 --> 00:19:35.700
You can only be disappointed

00:19:35.700 --> 00:19:38.100
if you have expectations

00:19:38.100 --> 00:19:40.680
that are different than the reality.

00:19:40.680 --> 00:19:43.140
My expectations are,

00:19:43.140 --> 00:19:48.140
that often celebrities will take advantage

00:19:48.450 --> 00:19:52.860
of their celebrity status
against vulnerable victims,

00:19:52.860 --> 00:19:56.340
and often against their own fans,

00:19:56.340 --> 00:19:59.760
which is very disturbing

00:19:59.760 --> 00:20:03.960
because I always feel that
celebrities and powerful people

00:20:03.960 --> 00:20:08.960
should feel very blessed about
the privileges that they have

00:20:09.570 --> 00:20:11.880
because they are celebrities.

00:20:11.880 --> 00:20:16.410
And I often say about
those celebrity attorneys

00:20:16.410 --> 00:20:20.490
who represent their clients
who are being accused,

00:20:20.490 --> 00:20:23.700
they represent the Hollywood bad boys,

00:20:23.700 --> 00:20:26.130
and I represent the women they hurt.

00:20:26.130 --> 00:20:27.390
Well, it definitely sounds like

00:20:27.390 --> 00:20:30.960
it's changed your whole view
of the world that we live in

00:20:30.960 --> 00:20:33.210
and given it a completely
different complexion.

00:20:33.210 --> 00:20:35.580
Just finally, in that
documentary about your life

00:20:35.580 --> 00:20:38.197
that I'm sure many people
will have seen on Netflix,

00:20:38.197 --> 00:20:40.260
in 2015 I believe,

00:20:40.260 --> 00:20:44.730
you said you'd had no
holidays in 40 years.

00:20:44.730 --> 00:20:46.530
Have you had one since?

00:20:46.530 --> 00:20:49.770
I'm hoping perhaps a glimmer
of a break here and there.

00:20:49.770 --> 00:20:53.640
Well, there's no holiday from injustice.

00:20:53.640 --> 00:20:54.930
Oh, come on, Gloria.

00:20:54.930 --> 00:20:57.478
Little bit, a little bit of a break?

00:20:57.478 --> 00:20:58.311
A little bit of a break.

00:20:58.311 --> 00:21:00.720
When I'm six feet under,
when that day comes,

00:21:00.720 --> 00:21:02.910
it will come for all of us.

00:21:02.910 --> 00:21:05.970
Maybe I'll have some rest at that time,

00:21:05.970 --> 00:21:10.800
although I am considering many ways

00:21:10.800 --> 00:21:13.890
that perhaps I can help
even from the grave,

00:21:13.890 --> 00:21:16.920
but we have to fight back for women.

00:21:16.920 --> 00:21:19.740
It's my duty.

00:21:19.740 --> 00:21:23.670
I am blessed to have the
privilege to help others

00:21:23.670 --> 00:21:27.150
to rise up, to become empowered.

00:21:27.150 --> 00:21:29.370
And that's what this is all about.

00:21:29.370 --> 00:21:32.820
And I do not need rest.

00:21:32.820 --> 00:21:35.610
If anything, we have a saying, Emma,

00:21:35.610 --> 00:21:39.843
that women become more
radical as they get older.

00:21:41.220 --> 00:21:44.100
The women's movement is unique

00:21:44.100 --> 00:21:47.340
on all movements in that way.

00:21:47.340 --> 00:21:50.430
And yes, I see even more need

00:21:50.430 --> 00:21:52.950
after 47 years of practicing law

00:21:52.950 --> 00:21:55.290
than I did when I began to practice.

00:21:55.290 --> 00:21:58.260
So I do have a passion for justice.

00:21:58.260 --> 00:22:00.780
I have no interest in holidays.

00:22:00.780 --> 00:22:04.170
I only have interest in winning justice,

00:22:04.170 --> 00:22:06.480
and that is what I will continue to do.

00:22:06.480 --> 00:22:08.010
Gloria, I like that.

00:22:08.010 --> 00:22:10.170
I look forward to
getting even more radical

00:22:10.170 --> 00:22:11.640
and busy as I get older.

00:22:11.640 --> 00:22:14.250
And that's because of our life experience.

00:22:14.250 --> 00:22:16.740
It's not because of any
women's studies class

00:22:16.740 --> 00:22:18.090
we've ever had.

00:22:18.090 --> 00:22:22.260
Women recognize what is
wrong in their lives.

00:22:22.260 --> 00:22:26.070
And a matter of fact, if
when I visit some women

00:22:26.070 --> 00:22:29.100
in nursing homes and old age homes,

00:22:29.100 --> 00:22:33.900
they pick up their canes and
they say, "Gloria, don't stop.

00:22:33.900 --> 00:22:37.650
When these men attack you, just
continue and fight harder."

00:22:37.650 --> 00:22:41.550
Those women know the truth
about their lives, Emma,

00:22:41.550 --> 00:22:44.490
and I am fighting for
all women, young, old

00:22:44.490 --> 00:22:46.620
I don't care their color, their religion,

00:22:46.620 --> 00:22:48.270
their ethnic origin.

00:22:48.270 --> 00:22:52.710
We want them to rise up and
become empowered and fight back,

00:22:52.710 --> 00:22:54.600
choose your battles carefully,

00:22:54.600 --> 00:22:58.470
but fight back and you can win justice.

00:22:58.470 --> 00:23:03.300
Well, on that, I think also
the idea of growing old,

00:23:03.300 --> 00:23:04.140
not disgracefully,

00:23:04.140 --> 00:23:07.770
but getting more angry
and more active is one.

00:23:07.770 --> 00:23:09.540
And it's often said women definitely

00:23:09.540 --> 00:23:11.970
made the personal political as well.

00:23:11.970 --> 00:23:14.490
Gloria Allred, thank you very much.

00:23:14.490 --> 00:23:15.330
Thank you, Emma.

00:23:15.330 --> 00:23:17.370
And thank you so much for being with us.

00:23:17.370 --> 00:23:19.923
Until we meet again,
take care and goodbye.

